# Direct runtime dependencies, hand-edited. `requirements.txt` is the
# fully-pinned lockfile GENERATED from this file -- never edit that one by
# hand; see docs/reproducible_builds.md.
#
# Upper bounds cap at the next MAJOR version: a minor/patch release is
# assumed backward-compatible per semver, a major release is not. This is a
# maintenance-burden tradeoff, not a correctness requirement -- tighten any
# of these to a minor-version cap (e.g. `pandas>=3.0,<3.1`) if a library's
# history shows breaking changes within a major version.
#
# playwright and python-dotenv were previously missing from this file
# entirely, even though scraper/full_auto_scrape.py and env_loader.py (the
# latter imported by nearly every entry point) import them directly -- a
# fresh clone running `pip install -r requirements.txt` alone could not
# actually run the scraper. Added here as real, direct dependencies.

